<title>NETHERLANDS: EU/Latam ministers call for end to Peru siege.</title>
<headline>EU/Latam ministers call for end to Peru siege.</headline>
<dateline>NOORDWIJK, Netherlands 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union and Latin American foreign ministers on Tuesday called for the immediate release of 72 hostages held by Tupac Amaru rebels at the Japanese embassy in Peru.</p>
<p>&quot;We vigorously condemn acts of terrorism ... and demand the immediate release of the hostages,&quot; said a statement by the 15 EU and 11 Latin American foreign ministers during a meeting at this Dutch seaside town.</p>
<p>&quot;We urge the government of Peru to spare no effort in attempting to find a peaceful solution to the problem,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>The siege of the embassy in Lima by the Marxist rebels entered its 113th day on Tuesday with still no sign of a breakthrough.</p>
</text>
